@* Plan C16 (pass 28b): a Gun, a tank's MA, a light mortar, a LATW, or a Panzerfaust fired at a Location or one vehicle in it. The page gives the
   firing side's weapons with their state in the label, the units the view sees for the Spotter and the leader (ruling R23.1), and the target
   fields' choices; choosing another weapon resets the ammunition, the Spotter, and the leader, and another target clears the vehicle, both in
   the page's handlers (section 15.3). The planner decides every shot. *@
<ActionSection Title="Ordnance" Key="ordnance">
<RuleHelp Id="ordnance-help" Summary="A manned Gun or a tank's MA fires HE at a Location's units, or the ammunition it carries at one vehicle there; a light mortar fires on the Area Target Type; a Panzerfaust or Panzerschreck fires HEAT, and an ATR AP, at a vehicle (C3.3, C3.31, C9.3, C13).">
    A Gun manned by its crew, or a tank's MA, fires HE at the enemy units of a Location on the Infantry Target Type (C3.3, C3.32), or at
    one enemy vehicle there on the Vehicle Target Type with AP, APCR, APDS, HEAT, or HE (C3.31, C8.1). Special Ammunition is listed with its
    Depletion Number at the game's date: an Original To Hit DR equal to it is the last such round, and above it the Gun had none and has not
    fired (C8.9); a Gun whose HE has such a number names it at Infantry too (C2.21, C8.8). A Gun that lists Canister fires it at one of the
    five vertices of its Covered Arc with no To Hit DR: one IFT DR attacks every hex that shares the vertex at the Gun's elevation and in its
    LOS, and the adjacent hex on the LOS at half FP, each with its own TEM and Hindrance, and is also the Depletion, malfunction, and ROF
    check (C8.4, C8.41). It turns its barrel or turret to bring the
    target into its Covered Arc if it must, with the Case A DRM (C5.1). An Original colored dr at most its ROF lets it fire again this
    phase (C2.24), and each shot acquires the Location for the next (C6.5). A hit on Infantry attacks every enemy unit there on the IFT
    column of the HE FP (C.6); a hit on a vehicle strikes its turret or hull, and the To Kill DR decides its fate (C3.9, C7). A light
    mortar fires on the Area Target Type at every unit of the hex, at half its HE FP, and may fire at a hex its Spotter in or next to its hex
    sees (C3.33, C9.3). From October 1943 a German unit may make a PF Check to fire a Panzerfaust at an enemy AFV (C13.31). An ATR fires
    AP at a vehicle here on the black Vehicle row up to 12 hexes, and at Infantry from the fire panel as 1 FP with no Long Range or Residual
    FP (C13.2, C13.24). A Panzerschreck, from September 1943, fires HEAT at a vehicle on its own table (10, 9, 8, 7 at 1 to 4 hexes), +2 from a
    ground-level building (not above it, nor pinned there), and is removed on 11 or 12 (C13.47, C13.8). Both are manufactured counters.
</RuleHelp>
<div class="toolbar">
    <label>
        Weapon
        <select id="ordnance-gun" value="@Gun" @onchange="@(args => OnGun.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? string.Empty))">
            <option value="">choose</option>
            @foreach (var gun in Guns)
            {
                <option value="@gun.Id">@Say(gun.Label)</option>
            }
        </select>
    </label>
    @if (Spotters is not null)
    {
        <label title="C9.3: a Good Order unit in the mortar's hex or an adjacent one spots for it (+2, ROF one less), in the PFPh or DFPh; it keeps spotting while Good Order.">
            Spotter
            <select id="ordnance-spotter" value="@Spotter" @onchange="@(args => OnSpotter.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? string.Empty))">
                <option value="">none</option>
                <UnitOptions Units="@Spotters" Text="@At" />
            </select>
        </label>
    }
    @if (Directors is not null)
    {
        <label title="A7.531: a leader in the firer's Location adds his leadership modifier to the To Hit DR, as his direction for the phase.">
            Leader
            <select id="ordnance-director" value="@Director" @onchange="@(args => OnDirector.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? string.Empty))">
                <option value="">none</option>
                @foreach (var leader in Directors)
                {
                    <option value="@leader.Id">@Say(leader.Label)</option>
                }
            </select>
        </label>
    }
    @Target
    @if (IntensiveAllowed)
    {
        <label title="C5.6: once its normal ROF is used, a Gun may fire once more with +2 (Case F) and its B# two lower; never in the AFPh."><input id="ordnance-intensive" type="checkbox" checked="@Intensive" @onchange="@(args => OnIntensive.InvokeAsync(args.Value is true))" /> Intensive Fire</label>
    }
    @if (PanzerfaustUsage is { } usage)
    {
        <span class="muted" id="ordnance-pf-usage">@usage</span>
    }
    <button id="propose-ordnance" disabled="@(!Ready)" aria-describedby="propose-ordnance-ready" @onclick="@(() => OnPropose.InvokeAsync())">Propose: fire</button>
    @if (!Ready)
    {
        <span id="propose-ordnance-ready" class="toolbar-note">@(ReadyNote ?? "Choose the weapon and its target, or its aim for Canister.")</span>
    }
</div>
</ActionSection>

@code {
    /// <summary>The page's words for the view (pass 31c, design D11): a unit's name for its id, a Location in words.</summary>
    [CascadingParameter(Name = "Say")]
    public Func<string, string>? Words { get; set; }

    private string Say(string? text) => text is null ? string.Empty : Words?.Invoke(text) ?? text;

    /// <summary>A unit's name with its hex, "4-6-7 squad G4 in [G4]" (the user, 2026-10-04), where no Location stands beside the name.</summary>
    [CascadingParameter(Name = "SayAt")]
    public Func<string, string>? WordsAt { get; set; }

    private string At(string? text) => text is null ? string.Empty : WordsAt?.Invoke(text) ?? Say(text);

    /// <summary>The firing side's Guns, tanks, light mortars, LATW, and Panzerfaust firers (whose value ends in ":pf").</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<PlayChoice> Guns { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public string Gun { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The units that may spot for a light mortar, or null when the weapon takes no Spotter.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<PlayChoice>? Spotters { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string Spotter { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The leaders who may direct the shot, or null when the weapon takes no leader.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<PlayChoice>? Directors { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string Director { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The target fields, an <see cref="OrdnanceTargetFields"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public RenderFragment Target { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>Whether the weapon may use Intensive Fire (a Gun or MA, not a mortar, LATW, or Panzerfaust).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool IntensiveAllowed { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public bool Intensive { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The side's Panzerfaust shots against its allowance, or null when it has no Panzerfaust firer.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? PanzerfaustUsage { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether a weapon and a target are chosen.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Ready { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What the shot still lacks, when it is not the weapon and target alone (a MG's AFV, A9.61; pass 60); null for the usual note.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? ReadyNote { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnGun { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnSpotter { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnDirector { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<bool> OnIntensive { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnPropose { get; set; }
}
